                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name from Irish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f6f69c6-84c1-40dd-a650-399282d4cd06",
                                                "sense_id": "9232f856-1719-364f-9f25-a71fed457edb",
                                                "text": "\"What the deuce is their fancy for calling the young beggar Brian?\" he inquired.\"Is it Brian Boroimhe they have gone back to, or is it some of her people, or what?\"\n\"There was a good Drewitt once,\" answered Wilhelmina, \"- - - and his name was Brian. - - - And Nannie told her, too, how a child always strains after the person it is called after, and how luck follows names, and worked her up to such a pit finally, that nothing would do her but the young gentleman must be called Brian and accordingly Brian he is - Brian Archibald. It is not an easy name to make fun out of; so all I can do is to call him Brin Baldy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a28c6bc-dc3f-4995-88d8-93d2ec557a8e",
                                                "sense_id": "9232f856-1719-364f-9f25-a71fed457edb",
                                                "text": "Why oh why had his parents even considered Brian? Brian is someone who works in a hardware shop or fixes the U bend. What chance did Sir Lovesdaslutalot have in life with a name like Brian? You can't even shorten Brian to Bri without it sounding like a kind of cheese!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "434dec15-b4f5-40d0-ba5b-c4882004af79",
                                                "sense_id": "9232f856-1719-364f-9f25-a71fed457edb",
                                                "text": "Chili’s has also enlisted several actors from “The Office” to star in the ads, including Melora Hardin (Jan Levinson), Andy Buckley (David Wallace), Brian Baumgartner (Kevin Malone) and Kate Flannery (Meredith Palmer)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
